<h2 id="what-is-gohighlevel">🏢 What Is GoHighLevel?</h2>

GoHighLevel (GHL) launched as an agency-focused white-label CRM platform and has evolved into a comprehensive business operating system. The platform consolidates CRM, marketing automation, appointment scheduling, reputation management, website building, and communication tools into a single dashboard.

For franchise operations, GHL's architecture offers something unique: the ability to create unlimited sub-accounts under one master account. Each franchisee gets their own isolated environment while corporate maintains oversight and control over brand standards, automated workflows, and reporting.

The platform competes directly with Salesforce, HubSpot, and franchise-specific solutions like FranConnect—but at a fraction of the cost. Where enterprise franchise CRMs run $200-500 per location monthly, GHL's unlimited model means your per-location cost decreases as you scale.

